{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/a-cut-opens-into-its-two-clips-walk",
  "seed": "Expand the Cut opens the cut between two clips into its two clips on rows of their own under V1, the way the transition walkthrough's step 5 draws it, at Next defaults with no flag set. The recording is cut down to six seconds and b-roll butted onto it, the cut picked and a one second cross dissolve put on it, then Option E: A ends on the cut and runs on half a second past it hatched, B starts on the cut and comes up half a second early hatched, and 'both on screen · 1.0s' sits over the second where both are on screen, every edge measured against the ruler within a point. Dip to black releases the overlap, a three second hold on black parts the two rows by the black, and Option E again closes them. Nothing moves a clip by opening the rows.",
